{
  "feature": "About The 99 \u2014 the reference page, its gate and its figures",
  "note": "Every figure gets its own row, addressed by NAME. Every entry carries a figure, and the sheet's job is the one a test cannot do: show that each frame holds something, at both widths, in one glance. Two rows either side photograph the page head and the destination state. The account-menu row is deliberately absent \u2014 every verb here reaches page content through `onPage`, which scopes to `<main>`, and the shell's account trigger sits outside it by construction; `account-menu.test.tsx` covers it instead. The two launch-entry rows need a server with their switches on; with them off those entries are not on the page and the rows fail, which is the absence this sheet exists to show.",
